      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Culinary History: \r\nA 20th century dish first served at a restaurant
    called Moti Mahal in \r\nDelhi 1947, fleeting India\u2019s partition. It is believed
    to have been invented by \r\nusing leftover tandoori chicken with a rich tomato,
    butter & cream sauce, \r\ntransforming leftovers into a dish that is popular
    within and outside of \r\nIndia. This dish is unique in many ways, but it is
    also the center of an on\x02going legal & court dispute over who deserves credit
    for its invention."
